== Effects ==
* While held, the last door Isaac went through stays open, allowing him to leave the room even if enemies are in it.
** Does not prevent doors from closing while Isaac is within the room, e.g. triggering a {{R|Challenge Room}} or awaking an Angel in an {{r|Angel Room}}.

== Notes ==
* Does not work in [[Greed Mode]].
** {{dlc|r}} Cannot spawn in Greed Mode.
* This trinket allows Isaac to leave rooms, including boss rooms, if the fight goes poorly.
** This becomes particularly useful in {{s|The Void}}, as it allows to escape the {{e|Delirium}} fight if encountered.
* Leaving immediately after enemies have spawned gives the player information on the fight, potentially improving decision making.
* If a {{R|Devil Room}} has a {{e|Krampus}} fight in it, Isaac may choose not to fight him and leave.
* If {{e|Greed}} / {{e|Super Greed}} is found in a {{R|Shop}}, one can kill it and leave the room while summoned monsters are still alive to respawn the boss and farm its loot infinitely.
* Does not affect {{e|Mom}}'s and {{e|Mega Satan}}'s boss room as the access door itself disappears.
* {{dlc|nr}} If a room contained champion enemies, upon leaving and re-entering the room, all previous champion enemies will have turned to regular enemies.

== Synergies ==
* {{A|Golden Trinket|r+}} / {{i|Mom's Box|r+}}: Boss Rush exit remains open.
* {{i|4.5 Volt}} / {{i|Jumper Cables}}: Provides infinite charges by clearing some enemies then leaving the room, and repeating.
* {{I|Charm of the Vampire}} / {{I|Gimpy}}: Allows the possibility to generate unlimited Hearts.
* {{I|Head of the Keeper}}: With enough patience, Coins can be gathered infinitely.
* {{i|Holy Mantle}}: Can be used to reset the shield at will.
* {{c|Tainted Keeper}}: Leaving and re-entering the room allows for limited coin farming; however, enemies in rooms Tainted Keeper has already visited will eventually stop dropping coins.

